What is Automotive Active Sound Control?
Automotive Active Sound Control (ASC) is an advanced audio-signal-processing technology designed to enhance or suppress cabin noise in real time. The system utilizes microphones, accelerometers, and vehicle reference signals (such as engine RPM and wheel speed) to generate counteracting sound waves ("anti-noise") or synthetic engine notes through speakers or dedicated actuators. ASC plays a critical role in improving acoustic comfort by canceling low-frequency road/engine noise or tailoring sound profiles for brand-specific driving experiences, particularly in electric and hybrid vehicles where traditional engine sounds are absent.

